<title>UK: Sweden sets $300 million December 2000 bond.</title>
<headline>Sweden sets $300 million December 2000 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWEDEN</p>
<p> AMT    $300 MLN	COUPON     6.25 PCT  MATURITY    04.DEC.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.26    PAY DATE  S-03.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    99.86     SPREAD	+5 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/SE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.4	 PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
